this thanksgiving will be a whole lot  different for many valley families eight  news now reporter salah jeremiah spoke  to some families  and stores businesses about the changes  they're making this year  with cover numbers being on the rise  many people i've spoken to have told me  that they have done their shopping  ahead of time and are relying on  pre-made meals in order to avoid those  large crowds  on thanksgiving yuri martin is the  general manager  at marie calendars every year they make  sure they have everything ready for  thanksgiving to make things  easier and convenient for shoppers and  this year is no different  thanksgiving feasts are available all  you have to do is reheat  they have been taking orders since  october 60 to 70 a day  martin says people started picking up  their meals as early as  monday we have a tent set up outside  where you can come and purchase the pies  we also have a canopy it says fees  that's where you pick up the fees  inside the restaurant you'll be able to  pick up individual dinners to go  or platters family platters we've got a  lot of people that are cooking  thanksgiving dinner  maybe for the first time tomorrow you  can't go to grandma's house you can't go  to mom's house and so  it's neat to see i think a lot of folks  are experimenting brian watcher with the  retail association of nevada says to  keep people socially distanced  there are staff at entrances counting  customers coming  and going now if you still haven't done  your shopping yet the retail association  of nevada wants to remind everyone  to make a list ahead of time so that you  can make your shopping experience a lot  smoother  quicker and safer reporting sally  jaramillo 8 news now  to avoid the holiday rush retailers and  small businesses  in nevada remind people to support local  business  use curbside pickup if you can along  with delivery services those businesses  need your help  statewide restrictions include wearing a  mask if you attend small family  gatherings we asked on twitter  will you follow this safety measure this  holiday 41 percent  say yes 59 percent say no
 

